Produce an execution-ready ownership and migration inventory for every backend-to-TUI path, starting with runtime.h, app/tui/interactive_tui.cpp and state_snapshot, runtime_state.*, runtime_active_run_internal.*, TuiFrontEnd.* and app/frontend/*. Cover initial options, callback/action results, selectors, settings, trust, overview, subagents, transcript/tool events, permissions/questions and plugin/image/Mermaid bridges. Trace producers and consumers, not just Snapshot names.

Classify by effect: UnlockedData is only for state that affects the backend and is or may become visible. Prominently cover the active agent receiving the next Enter submission, model/provider/variant and execution reasoning settings, directories especially workspace root, and used tokens. Establish the true selected-agent owner, selection writers and tests rather than inferring authority from UI labels. Record owners, writers, lifecycle, projections, coherence, authority and coverage. Pure appearance/interaction state belongs in src/ava/tui, app/tui or tui-named files, on the tui-thread without locks or UnlockedData. Draft text stays exclusively frontend-owned until submitted as a string. Distinguish reasoning execution from reasoning display and backend attachment authority from image-render preferences. Confirm ModelSelection and SessionStats as the reference mechanism without extending it to UI-only state.

Store source-backed inventory and acceptance artifacts with contents entries, accounting for every transfer and concrete focused/terminal verification. Explicitly preserve existing history/streaming and applicable history-inspector/picker content transport this iteration: history is too large to snapshot and future backend list/vector access needs separate design. Enumerate retained paths and existing authority/ordering checks; neither remove functionality nor design a new journal or history migration. The exception cannot shelter unrelated backend facts. Resolve ownership ambiguities before coding; renaming a snapshot is not migration.
